// MP -- message passing, release-acquire, without the paper's spin loop.
//
// Source: Arlt & Vafeiadis, "RGSep under Release/Acquire Consistency",
//         PACMPL 10 (OOPSLA2), Article 375, 2026. doi:10.1145/3839507, Section 3.
//
// The paper's reader spins on y before reading x (MP-repeat.lit); here it reads
// y once, and the outcome of interest is the one where it read 1. Under RA the
// assertion b = 7 holds; the paper notes it fails under the relaxed fragment of
// C11 (MP+rlx.lit) and under strong coherence (SCOH), which is why RGSep is
// unsound under those models.
//
// Reference verdicts:
//   the paper: under RA, reading y = 1 implies x = 7.
//   herd7 7.58 on herd/MP.litmus, under the zoo's abstract-sc, abstract-tso,
//     ra, sra, wra and abstract-coherence cat models and herd's rc11.cat:
//     Coherence allows; SC, TSO, RA, SRA, WRA and RC11 forbid.
// The paper's registers are renamed r -> ry, b -> rb:
// MoRDor reads only names beginning with r as registers.
x := 0; y := 0;
{ x.store(7, rel); y.store(1, rel) }
||| { ry := y.load(acq); rb := x.load(acq) }
%%
allow (ry = 1 && rb != 7) [Coherence]
forbid (ry = 1 && rb != 7) [SC, TSO, RA, SRA, WRA, RC11]
